# Landflow core

- Product: Landflow, SaaS website builder focused on automotive sites.
- UI text is Russian only. Code/database/type identifiers stay English.
- Stack: Laravel + React + Inertia + TypeScript + shadcn/ui + Tailwind + npm.
- Use PHPUnit, Larastan/PHPStan, Pint, vite-plus/Vite and Playwright already present. Do not add competing tooling by default.
- `Workspace` is the tenant; `User` is identity; `Site` belongs to a Workspace.
- Backend is authoritative for tenancy, authorization, permissions, entitlements, prices and secrets.
- Global catalog is platform-owned; customer changes never mutate canonical global data.
- Draft and Published are separate; autosave never publishes.
- Never expose secrets to React, published output, logs or exports.
- Never perform production deploy/DNS/billing/destructive production actions without explicit approval.
- Never force-push.

## Lean execution

For backlog work, follow `.cursor/rules/90-agent-workflow.mdc` and `docs/automation/AUTONOMOUS_WORKFLOW.md`.
Default: one Agent, targeted context, targeted tests, no subagents unless a risk trigger requires one.
Do not read the whole docs tree before ordinary tasks.
Use `BACKLOG.md`, `PROJECT_STATE.md`, `DECISIONS.md` plus only task-relevant architecture docs.
If an approved ADR/product decision is required and unresolved, stop with `BLOCKED_DECISION`.
